<title>INDIA: India produces 2.60 mln tonnes sugar in February.</title>
<headline>India produces 2.60 mln tonnes sugar in February.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>India produced 2.60 million tonnes of sugar in February, 1997, slightly down from 2.65 million tonnes in the same month in the previous year, the sugar industry said on Monday.</p>
<p>In a joint statement the Indian Sugar Mills Association and the National Federation of Cooperative Sugar Factories said output during the five months of the 1996/97 (October-September) season totalled 8.23 million tonnes compared with 9.13 million tonnes in the year ago period.</p>
<p>The statement said India held 9.98 million tonnes of sugar on February 28, 1997, compared with 8.88 million tonnes on the same date in 1996.</p>
</text>
